                <pb facs="0571" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/2784: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-18T09:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 18,
                                1923—9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:03 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>105. Referring to my telegram of December 17, 2 p.m. By Executive decree martial
                    law has been declared throughout the Republic.</p>
                <p>Fourteen Carias adherents were placed under arrest at Amapala last evening.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
